{
  "title": "Sahifa Sajjadiya 33: Asking for the Best (Istikhara)",
  "data": "اللَّهُمَّ اِنِيِّ اَسْتَخِيرُكَ بِعِلْمِكَ، فَصَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَاقْضِ لِي بِالْخِيَرَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INIYYI ASTAKHEERUKA BI-I'LMIKA FASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WAQDI LEE BIL KHIYARAH\nO God, I ask from Thee the best in Thy knowledge, so bless Muhammad and his Household and decree for me the best!\nوَاَلْهِمْنَا مَعْرِفَةَ الِاخْتِيَارِ، وَاجْعَلْ ذٰلِكَ ذَرِيعَةً اِلَى الرِّضَا بِمَا قَضَيْتَ لَنَا وَالتَّسْلِيمِ لِمَا حَكَمْتَ فَاَزِحْ عَنَّا رَيْبَ الِارْتِيَابِ، وَاَيِّدْنَا بِيَقِينِ الْمُخْلِصِينَ\nWA ALHIMNAA MA'RIFATAL IKHTIYAARI WAJ'AL DHAALIKA DHAREE'ATAN ILAR RIDAA BIMAA QADAYTA LANAA WAT TASLEEMI LIMAA HAKAMTA FA-AZIH A'NNAA RAYBAL IRTIYAABI WA AYYIDNAA BIYAQEENIL MUKHLISEEN\nInspire us with knowledge to chose the best and make that a means to being pleased with what Thou hast decreed for us and submitting to what Thou hast decided! Banish from us the doubt of misgiving and confirm us with the certainty of the sincere!\nوَلَا تَسُمْنَا عَجْزَ الْمَعْرِفَةِ عَمَّا تَخَيَّرْتَ فَنَغْمِطَ قَدْرَكَ، وَنَكْرَهَ مَوْضِعَ رِضَاكَ، وَنَجْنَحَ اِلَى الَّتِي هِيَ اَبْعَدُ مِنْ حُسْنِ الْعَاقِبَةِ، وَاَقْرَبُ اِلَى ضِدِّ الْعَافِيَةِ،\nWA LAA TASUMNAA A'JZAL MA'RIFATI A'MMAA TAKHAYYARTA FANAGHMITA QADRAKA WA NAKRAHA MAWDI'A RIDAAKA WA NAJNAHA ILAL LATEE HIYA AB'ADU MIN HUSNIL A'AQIBATI WA AQRABU ILAA DIDDIL A'AFIYAH\nVisit us not with incapacity to know what Thou hast chosen, lest we despise Thy measuring out, dislike the place of Thy good pleasure, and incline toward that which is further from good outcome and nearer to the opposite of well-being!\nحَبِّبْ اِلَيْنَا مَا نَكْرَهٗ مِنْ قَضَائِكَ، وَسَهِّلْ عَلَيْنَا مَا نَسْتَصْعِبُ مِنْ حُكْمِكَ\nHABBIB ILAYNAA MAA NAKRAHOO MIN QADAA'IKA WA SAHHIL A'LAYNAA MAA NASTAS'IBU MIN HUKMIK\nMake us love what we dislike in Thy decree and make easy for us what we find difficult in Thy decision!\nوَاَلْهِمْنَا الِانْقِيَادَ لِمَا اَوْرَدْتَ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ مَشِيَّتِكَ حَتَّى لَا نُحِبَّ تَاْخِيرَ مَا عَجَّلْتَ، وَلَا تَعْجِيلَ مَا اَخَّرْتَ، وَلَا نَكْرَهَ مَا اَحْبَبْتَ، وَلَا نَتَخَيَّرَ مَا كَرِهْتَ\nWA ALHIMNAL INQIYAADA LIMAA AWRADTA A'LAYNAA MIN MASHIYYATIKA HATTAA LAA NUHIBBA TA'KHEERA MAA A'JJALTA WA LAA TA'JEELA MAA AKHKHARTA WA LAA NAKRAHA MAA AHBABTA WA LAA NATAKHAYYARA MAA KARIHT\nInspire us to yield to that which Thou bringest upon us by Thy will, lest we love the delay of what Thou hast hastened and the hastening of what Thou hast delayed, dislike what Thou lovest, and choose what Thou dislikest!\nوَاخْتِمْ لَنَا بِالَّتِي هِيَ اَحْمَدُ عَاقِبَةً، وَاَكْرَمُ مَصِيراً، اِنَّكَ تُفِيدُ الْكَرِيمَةَ، وَتُعْطِي الْجَسِيمَةَ، وَتَفْعَلُ مَا تُرِيدُ، وَاَنْتَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ\nWAKHTIM LANAA BILLATEE HIYA AHMADU A'AQIBATAN WA AKRAMU MASEERAN INNAKA TUFEEDUL KAREEMATA WA TU'TIL JASEEMATA WA TAF'ALU MAA TUREEDU WA ANTA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nSeal us with that which is most praised in outcome and most generous in issue! Surely Thou givest generous gain, bestowest the immense, dost what Thou wilt, and Thou art powerful over everything.",
  "merits": "The thirty-third supplication of al-Sahifah al-Kamilah al-Sajjadiyyah: Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s supplication in asking Allah for the best (istikhara).\n\nEnglish translation by William C. Chittick."
}
